  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "A mountain stands high above the clouds. On the peak sits a mirror-like pond that reflects the traces of clouds in the sky and stays calm without ripples.",
      "chapters": [
        747
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Above the peak pond, Yuan tribe’s first supreme elder, a rank seven Gu Immortal with peak battle strength, practices spear methods while true martial carps under the water criticize his form. Those carps are mutated beast kings born from heaven and earth, white-skinned with black scales and no other color. When he leaves for an auction, he draws Human Language Immortal Gu from the pond so the carps’ speech ends, then flies away as light. Yuan Chi then covers the pond with thick white cloud, concealing an important place in Yuan tribe territory.",
      "chapters": [
        747
